%% Delegation contract: admission returns a handle, answers arrive as messages. Expect width.
sequenceDiagram
    participant P as Parent model
    participant H as Host (L7)
    participant K as Child runtime
    participant M as Provider
    P->>H: spawn("review API", name="api")
    H->>H: check RLM_DEPTH < MAX (default 2)
    H->>K: create child AgentSession + session_dir
    H-->>P: handle {id, name, session_dir, model}
    Note over P: admission only - the answer NEVER comes back here
    P->>H: spawn("review tests", name="tests")
    H-->>P: handle  (fan out, then END THE TURN)
    K->>M: child loop streams independently
    M-->>K: response / tool calls
    K->>H: agent_message.send(msg, receiver_role=parent)
    H-->>P: arrives as an ordinary message, next turn
    H->>H: child_usage_attributed -> parent assistant turn
    Note over H: tree view subtracts it: own-context vs billable both reconcile
